---
layout: layouts/page.njk
permalink: /data/
lang: en
title: Open data on AI chatbots and Russian disinformation
description: Download the Sitera claim registry, chatbot observations, domain watchlist and escalation log as CSV and JSON under CC BY 4.0, with citation.
h1: Data
schemas:
  - datacatalog
breadcrumbTrail:
  - title: Home
    url: /
  - title: Data
    url: /data/
---
{% set doc = copy.en.data %}
<p class="lede">{{ doc.introText }}</p>

{% if datasets.all | length %}
<h2 id="downloads">Downloads</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <caption>Every dataset published from this site. All under CC BY 4.0.</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr><th scope="col">Dataset</th><th scope="col">Format</th><th scope="col">What it contains</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for item in datasets.all %}
    <tr>
      <th scope="row"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.name }}</a></th>
      <td>{{ item.format }}</td>
      <td>{{ item.description }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% for id in doc.order %}
{% set section = doc.sections[id] %}
<h2 id="{{ section.id }}">{{ section.title }}</h2>
{{ section.html | safe }}
{% endfor %}

<h2 id="cite">How to cite</h2>
<p class="cite-block">{{ site.org.name }} ({{ site.last_update | year }}). Registry of Russian disinformation in AI chatbot answers. Version {{ site.watchlist_version }}. {{ site.url }}/data/</p>
<p class="cite-block">@misc{ {{- site.org.name | lower }}{{ site.last_update | year }},
  author = { {{- site.org.name -}} },
  title  = {Registry of Russian disinformation in AI chatbot answers},
  year   = { {{- site.last_update | year -}} },
  url    = { {{- site.url }}/data/}
}</p>
<p>Questions about the data, or a request for extended access: <a href="mailto:{{ site.org.email.research }}">{{ site.org.email.research }}</a></p>
